  "answer": "I'll look through the storefront cart API and how store merchant settings are read so the quantity limit can be applied without a restart.The limit belongs in the cart facade, read from merchant configuration on each request so a store can change it without a restart. I'll reject any line over that limit before the cart is saved.The storefront cart create, add, and update paths now read `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY` from the store's merchant configuration on every request (default 99) and reject any line that would go above that limit with HTTP 400 before the cart is saved. A quantity of 0 still removes the line.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am test -Dtest=CartLineQuantityLimitTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 from the live cart endpoints and that a rejected request leaves the stored cart unchanged\"], \"missing\": [\"an integration test or fixture that sets CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY and calls POST /api/v1/cart, PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}, and POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi\"]}",
